hexagon: saturate the FP16 tile scales of the Q4_K and Q6_K repack
Fold-into: upstream/hexagon-host

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

The repack of Q4_K and Q6_K into the tiled layout of the DSP writes each
product of the block scale and a sub-block scale as an FP16 value. A product
above 65504 became Inf in the tile, and the DSP multiplied with Inf. The read
back divides the sub-block scales by the block scale, and for an Inf or NaN
ratio it converted NaN to an integer, which is undefined behavior.

This patch saturates each FP16 scale of the tile to +-65504 and writes 0 for
NaN. The read back gives 0 for a ratio that is not finite, and rounds and
clamps each other ratio to the range of its field. A product in the FP16
range gives the same bytes as before, thus the repacked bytes of real weights
do not change.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp
index 70f1d61..53d0f4a 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp
@@ -1530,6 +1530,23 @@ static inline uint8_t q6_K_get_quant(const block_q6_K * b, int e) {
